WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.200
Since 2016, when I got saved,

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.740
I've been studying the Bible.

3
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.290
And it was all scattered.

4
00:00:11.213 --> 00:00:13.033
So I made my own Bible notes app.

5
00:00:13.073 --> 00:00:15.653
Harvous is the one I've been wanting.

6
00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:18.304
Every day starts here.

7
00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:21.684
There's a passage waiting, and whatever I was

8
00:00:21.724 --> 00:00:24.064
in the middle of, so I can pick right back up.

9
00:00:24.104 --> 00:00:25.904
On my laptop, or on my phone.

10
00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:33.603
When I write, Harvous knows Scripture.

11
00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:37.183
I type a reference, and it becomes

12
00:00:37.223 --> 00:00:38.882
the verse, right there in my note.

13
00:00:40.825 --> 00:00:44.185
Tap a reference, and the passage opens right

14
00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:47.305
on the page, and stays put as I scroll.

15
00:00:47.605 --> 00:00:50.565
Cross-references are a tap away.

16
00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:53.105
So is every note I've written on it.

17
00:00:53.165 --> 00:00:55.345
And if a word catches me, the

18
00:00:55.385 --> 00:00:56.585
dictionary's right there.

19
00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:01.585
And when I open the Bible, those

20
00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:03.525
same notes sit in the margin,

21
00:01:03.585 --> 00:01:05.265
beside the verses they're about.

22
00:01:05.305 --> 00:01:08.244
Over time, it becomes my own study Bible.

23
00:01:14.068 --> 00:01:15.527
I never have to file anything.

24
00:01:15.568 --> 00:01:18.648
Harvous tags my notes, and sorts

25
00:01:18.688 --> 00:01:20.667
them into folders, on its own.

26
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.600
And threads are mine.

27
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.680
I pull one theme together, across

28
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.920
weeks of study, like everything I've

29
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.580
been learning about the Holy Spirit.

30
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.260
I can share the whole thread with a link.

31
00:01:36.788 --> 00:01:40.108
And each note links to the others, so

32
00:01:40.148 --> 00:01:42.288
I can walk the whole line of thinking.

33
00:01:46.918 --> 00:01:48.898
And the part I care about most.

34
00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:50.378
Harvous brings my study

35
00:01:50.418 --> 00:01:52.318
back, so it actually sticks.

36
00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:53.898
Not just what I read, but

37
00:01:53.938 --> 00:01:55.658
what I wrote about it.

38
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.420
That's how I study, most days.

39
00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.340
And there's more.

40
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.800
Templates to start a study.

41
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.440
Translations side by side.

42
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.960
A shared space for your group.

43
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.000
A family plan, with notebooks for your kids.

44
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.400
And features for churches are coming soon.

45
00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.530
Right now, it's just me working on Harvous.

46
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.070
God willing, there'll be a small team one day.

47
00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.450
Until then, if you have any questions

48
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.470
or feedback, please reach out.

49
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.790
I'd love to hear from you.

